      LessonBlock.heading("Ye lesson kyun zaroori hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Level 1 me tum ne har hisse ko alag alag pehchanna seekha tha. Ab Level 2 me paper tum se wohi pehchan aik hi jumle ke andar karwata hai. One paper me is par seedha sawal ata hai ke is jumle me ye lafz kis part of speech hai. Sawal dekhne me chhota lagta hai, lekin phansata bohat hai, kyunke paper wale jan bujh kar wo lafz dete hain jo do hisso ka kaam karta hai. Water kabhi noun hai aur kabhi verb. Fast kabhi adjective hai aur kabhi adverb. Jo student lafz ko nahi, us ke kaam ko pehchanta hai, wo ye number kabhi nahi khota. Ye lesson tumhe wahi nazar dega. Aakhir tak tum kisi bhi jumle ke har lafz ka kaam bata sako ge, aur yehi skill aage narration aur sentence wale lessons ki buniyad hai."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Aath hisse, aik hi khandan"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Dekho, English ka har jumla alfaaz se banta hai, aur har lafz jumle me koi na koi kaam kar raha hota hai. Ussi kaam ke hisaab se alfaaz ko aath hisso me baanta gaya hai. In aath hisso ko parts of speech kehte hain. Ye aath naam ratne wali cheez nahi hain. Ye aik khandan ke aath afrad hain, aur har aik ka apna kaam hai. Kaam pehchan lo, naam khud yaad ho jayega."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Pehla hissa noun hai. Ye naam wala hai. Shakhs, jagah, cheez ya khayal ka naam. Ali, Lahore, kitaab, mohabbat. Ye hum Lesson 1 me tafseel se parh chuke hain. Doosra hissa pronoun hai. Ye noun ka naib hai. Noun ki jagah ata hai taake naam bar bar na dohrana pare. I, you, he, she, it, we, they, aur in ki dusri shaklein me, him, her, us, them. Ye hum Lesson 3 aur Lesson 14 me parh chuke hain. Teesra hissa verb hai. Ye jumle ka dil hai. Kaam ya halat batata hai. Run, write, eat, aur is, am, are, was, were bhi verb hi hain, kyunke ye halat batate hain. Chautha hissa adjective hai. Ye noun ya pronoun ki khoobi ya khami batata hai, us ki miqdar ya ginti batata hai. Brave, honest, five, some, this. Ye hum Lesson 8 me parhna shuru kiya tha aur Lesson 27 me is ki saari qismein ayengi. Panchwan hissa adverb hai. Ye verb ki, adjective ki ya kisi dusre adverb ki khoobi batata hai. Quickly, very, yesterday, here. Chhata hissa preposition hai. Ye rabta wala hai. Noun ya pronoun ka rishta jumle ke baqi hisse se jorta hai. In, on, at, under, between. Ye hum Lesson 5 me parh chuke hain. Saatwan hissa conjunction hai. Ye jorne wala hai. Do alfaaz, do hisse ya do jumle jorta hai. And, but, or, because, although. Aathwan aur aakhri hissa interjection hai. Ye achanak jazbaat wala hai. Wah, alas, hurrah, oh. Ye jumle ke grammar se alag khara hota hai, bas dil ki awaaz hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab aik aham baat zehen me bitha lo. Lafz ka hissa us ki surat se nahi, jumle me us ke kaam se tay hota hai. Yehi is poore lesson ki jaan hai, aur yehi paper ka sab se bara jaal hai."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Aik lafz, kai kirdaar"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab wo baat jo paper me sab se zyada phansati hai. Aik hi lafz mukhtalif jumlo me mukhtalif hisse ban sakta hai. Water ko dekho. The water of this well is cold. Yahan water cheez ka naam hai, noun hai. Ab doosra jumla. Please water the plants in the evening. Yahan water aik kaam hai, pani dena. Ye verb hai. Lafz wahi, kaam badal gaya, hissa badal gaya."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Love bhi aisa hi hai. Love is a noble feeling. Yahan love khayal ka naam hai, noun hai. I love my country. Yahan love kaam hai, verb hai. Book bhi. This book is very interesting. Yahan book noun hai. He books his ticket in advance. Yahan books ka matlab hai ticket karwana, ye verb hai. Fast ka jaal aur bhi mashhoor hai. He is a fast bowler. Yahan fast bowler ki khoobi bata raha hai, adjective hai. He ran fast. Yahan fast daurne ke tareeqe ko bata raha hai, adverb hai. Aur yaad rakho, fast ka adverb fast hi hota hai. Fastly naam ki koi cheez English me nahi hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Since bhi do kaam karta hai. He has been ill since Monday. Yahan since aik waqt se rabta jor raha hai, preposition hai. Since he was ill, he stayed at home. Yahan since do jumlo ko jor raha hai aur wajah bata raha hai, conjunction hai. Round bhi kai kirdaar nibhata hai, lekin paper ke liye ye teen misaalein, water, fast aur since, sab se zyada aham hain. Usool aik hi hai. Lafz ko mat dekho, ye dekho ke wo jumle me kar kya raha hai."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Board par qanoon Angrezi me"),
      LessonBlock.rule("Ustad board par aath hisso ki tareef yun likhta hai. A noun is the name of a person, place, thing or idea. A pronoun is a word used in place of a noun. A verb is a word that shows action or state. An adjective is a word that describes a noun or a pronoun. An adverb is a word that describes a verb, an adjective or another adverb. A preposition is a word that shows the relation of a noun or a pronoun with another word in the sentence. A conjunction is a word that joins words, phrases or sentences. An interjection is a word that shows a sudden feeling. Aur sab ke aakhir me ustad ye line moti kar ke likhta hai: the part of speech of a word depends on the work it does in the sentence, not on its form. Isi aik line par is lesson ke saare number hain."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Misaalein board se"),
