  Lesson(
    id: "grammar-26",
    number: 26,
    title: "Noun and Its Types",
    subtitle: "Noun aur us ki qismein. Khaas, aam, jamaat, jazbaat aur jins",
    partIndex: 1,
    partName: "Noun aur Pronoun — Gehraai",
    blocks: <LessonBlock>[
      LessonBlock.heading("Ye lesson kyun zaroori hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Lesson 1 me tum ne seekha tha ke noun har naam wali cheez ko kehte hain. Ab paper us se aik kadam aage jata hai. Paper poochhta hai ke ye noun kis qism ka hai. Proper hai ya common, collective hai ya abstract. Aur is se bhi aage, collective noun ke sath verb singular ayega ya plural, ye sawal one paper me bar bar ata hai. Committee has ya committee have, jury its ya jury their, yehi wo bareek jagah hai jahan tayyari wala student number leta hai aur rata lagane wala reh jata hai. Is lesson me hum paanch qismein aisi pakki karenge ke pehchan bhi ho jaye aur verb wala masla bhi hamesha ke liye hal ho jaye."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Paanch qismein, paanch pehchan"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Pehli qism proper noun hai. Ye kisi khaas shakhs, khaas jagah ya khaas cheez ka apna naam hota hai. Ali, Lahore, Pakistan, Quaid-e-Azam, the Indus. Is ki pehchan asan hai. Ye hamesha bare harf, capital letter, se shuru hota hai, aur ye sirf aik ka hai, poori qism ka nahi. Boy aam hai, lekin Ali khaas hai. City aam hai, lekin Lahore khaas hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Doosri qism common noun hai. Ye aik poori qism ka aam naam hota hai. Boy, city, book, teacher, river. Ye har us fard par lagta hai jo us qism ka ho. Koi bhi larka boy hai, koi bhi sheher city hai. Proper aur common ka farq sirf itna hai ke aik naam aik ka hai aur doosra naam sab ka hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Teesri qism collective noun hai. Ye meri pasandeeda qism hai kyunke yehi paper ka jaal hai. Ye aik lafz hota hai, lekin us ke andar poora group chhupa hota hai. Team gyarah khilariyon ka group hai, lekin lafz aik hai. Army, committee, jury, crowd, family, class, government, audience, flock, bunch, public. Aik lafz, poori jamaat. Ye pehchan yaad rakho, kyunke verb wala qanoon isi par chalta hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Chauthi qism abstract noun hai. Ye un cheezon ke naam hain jo mehsoos hoti hain, lekin ankh se dikhti nahi aur hath se chhui nahi jatin. Honesty, bravery, happiness, childhood, poverty, beauty, knowledge, freedom. Tum mohabbat ko dekh nahi sakte, bas mehsoos kar sakte ho. Ye hum Lesson 1 me khayal wale naam ke tor par parh chuke hain, abstract usi ka proper naam hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Panchvi qism material noun hai. Ye us cheez ka naam hai jis se dusri cheezein banti hain. Gold, silver, iron, wood, cotton, milk, water, wheat. Anguthi cheez hai, lekin gold wo jins hai jis se anguthi bani. Is qism ka apna qanoon hai. Ye aam tor par na gini jati hai, na is par a ya an ata hai, aur na hi is ki plural banti hai. Golds kehna ghalat hai."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Collective noun aur verb ka masla"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab is lesson ka sab se aham hissa. Collective noun ke sath verb kab singular aur kab plural? Qanoon ye hai. Jab jamaat aik jaan ho kar, aik unit ban kar kaam kare, to verb singular ata hai aur pronoun its ata hai. Jab jamaat ke log alag alag soch rahe hon ya alag alag kaam kar rahe hon, to verb plural ata hai aur pronoun their ata hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Misaal se samjho. The committee has submitted its report. Yahan committee ne aik ho kar report di hai. Aik unit hai, is liye has aur its. Ab doosri surat. The committee are divided in their opinion. Yahan members ki raye alag alag hai. Jamaat aik nahi rahi, log alag ho gaye, is liye are aur their. Jury par bhi yehi qanoon hai. The jury has given its verdict. Faisla aik hai, jamaat aik hai. Lekin the jury were divided in their opinion me har member apni jagah khara hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Paper is me is tarah phansata hai ke jumle ke do hisse mila deta hai. The committee has given their report. Ye ghalat hai, kyunke has singular hai aur their plural. Ya dono singular rakho, has aur its, ya dono plural, have aur their. Aadha idhar aadha udhar, yehi ghalti hai. Aur public par bhi nazar rakho. Public aam tor par logo ke majmue ke tor par plural verb leta hai, lekin jab wo aik idare ki tarah baat kare to singular bhi ata hai. Paper me jo hissa jumle me pehle se diya ho, verb usi ke hisaab se chunna hai."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Abstract aur material ke chhote qanoon"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Abstract noun ke sath sab se aam ghalti a ya an lagana hai. A honesty, an advice jaisi ghaltiyan Urdu soch se ati hain. Yaad rakho, jo cheez gini nahi ja sakti, us ke sath a ya an nahi ata. Advice par ye ghalti hum Lesson 13 me bhi dekh chuke hain, kyunke advice uncountable bhi hai aur abstract bhi. Haan, aik bareek baat aur hai. Kuch abstract nouns ke sath jab koi khoobi jude to article kabhi kabhi aa sakta hai, lekin paper ki satah par tum bas ye yaad rakho ke akela abstract noun article nahi leta."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Material noun ka qanoon is se bhi seedha hai. Ye wazan aur miqdar se naapa jata hai, gina nahi jata. Two golds ghalat hai, two grams of gold sahi hai. Aur jab kisi khaas cheez ki taraf ishara ho to the aa sakta hai. The gold of this ring is pure. Yahan gold aam jins nahi, is anguthi ka gold hai, is liye the aya."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Board par qanoon Angrezi me"),
      LessonBlock.rule("Ustad board par paanch qismo ki tareef yun likhta hai. A proper noun is the name of a particular person, place or thing, and it begins with a capital letter. A common noun is the name of a whole class or kind. A collective noun is the name of a group of persons or things taken as one whole. An abstract noun is the name of a quality, state or idea that can only be felt, not seen or touched. A material noun is the name of the substance from which things are made. Aur collective ke liye ustad alag se ye line likhta hai: a collective noun takes a singular verb when the group acts as one unit, and a plural verb when the members act separately. Ye line is lesson ki sab se qeemti line hai."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Misaalein board se"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab board par misaalein likhta hun. Har jumle me noun ki qism pehchano."),
      LessonBlock.example("Quaid-e-Azam was a great leader of the Muslims.", note: "Quaid-e-Azam proper noun hai, khaas shakhs ka naam. Leader common noun hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("The army marched into the city at night.", note: "Army collective noun hai. Poori fouj aik lafz me aa gayi."),
      LessonBlock.example("The committee has submitted its report to the minister.", note: "Committee collective hai, aur yahan wo aik unit hai, is liye has aur its aya."),
      LessonBlock.example("The committee are divided in their opinion about the new rules.", note: "Wahi committee, lekin yahan members alag alag hain, is liye are aur their aya. Farq lafz ka nahi, matlab ka hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Honesty of the officer impressed everyone in the office.", note: "Honesty abstract noun hai. Dikhti nahi, mehsoos hoti hai."),
