  Lesson(
    id: "grammar-31",
    number: 31,
    title: "All 12 Tenses — Pehchan aur Farq",
    subtitle: "Barah Tenses. Aik hi kahani, barah waqt, aur har tense ki pehchan",
    partIndex: 3,
    partName: "Verb aur Tenses",
    blocks: <LessonBlock>[
      LessonBlock.heading("Ye lesson kyun zaroori hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("PPSC ke one paper me tense ka sawal sab se zyada ane wale sawalon me se hai. Kabhi jumla de kar poocha jata hai ke ye konsa tense hai, kabhi khali jagah me sahi verb lagana hota hai, aur kabhi chaar jumlo me se aik theek jumla chunna hota hai. In teeno soraton me jeet usi ki hoti hai jo tense ko pehchan sakta hai. Masla ye hai ke aksar students barah tenses ko barah alag cheezein samajh kar ratte hain aur paper me sab gadh madh ho jata hai. Is lesson me hum barah tenses ko aik hi kahani par chala kar dekhenge, har tense ki pehchan wali nishani seekhenge, aur Urdu tarjume se tense pehchanne ka wo tareeqa seekhenge jo kabhi dhoka nahi deta. Lesson 18 me hum ne Past Tense ko tafseel se parha tha aur Lesson 19 me continuous wale rang dekhe thay. Ab un sab ko aik jagah jama karke poori tasveer dekhte hain."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Aik kahani, teen waqt"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Sab se pehle ye samajh lo ke tense asal me sirf teen hain. Maazi, yani past. Haal, yani present. Aur mustaqbil, yani future. Waqt bas ye teen hain. Phir har waqt ki chaar soratein hain. Kaam seedha sada bayan ho to simple. Kaam chal raha ho to continuous. Kaam mukammal ho chuka ho to perfect. Aur kaam aik muddat se chal raha ho to perfect continuous. Teen waqt gunah chaar soratein, kul barah tense. Bas, barah ka ye hisaab zehen me bitha lo, aadha bojh yahin utar gaya."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab Ali ki kahani suno. Ali kitaab parhta hai, aur hum usi aik kaam ko barah waqton me ghuma kar dekhte hain. Present simple me Ali roz kitaab parhta hai. Ali reads a book every day. Present continuous me Ali is waqt kitaab parh raha hai. Ali is reading a book now. Present perfect me Ali kitaab parh chuka hai. Ali has read the book. Present perfect continuous me Ali subah se kitaab parh raha hai. Ali has been reading the book since morning. Dekha tum ne? Waqt wohi haal hai, lekin kaam ki sorat har dafa badal gayi. Kabhi aadat, kabhi chal raha kaam, kabhi mukammal kaam, kabhi muddat se chal raha kaam."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab yahi kahani maazi me le jao. Past simple me Ali ne kal kitaab parhi. Ali read the book yesterday. Past continuous me jab main kamre me aya to Ali kitaab parh raha tha. Ali was reading a book when I entered the room. Past perfect me mere ane se pehle Ali kitaab parh chuka tha. Ali had read the book before I came. Past perfect continuous me Ali do ghante se kitaab parh raha tha. Ali had been reading the book for two hours. Aur ab mustaqbil. Future simple me Ali kal kitaab parhega. Ali will read the book tomorrow. Future continuous me Ali is waqt kal kitaab parh raha hoga. Ali will be reading a book at this time tomorrow. Future perfect me Ali itvaar tak kitaab parh chuka hoga. Ali will have read the book by Sunday. Future perfect continuous me Ali aath baje tak teen ghante se kitaab parh raha hoga. Ali will have been reading the book for three hours by eight o clock. Barah tense mukammal. Kahani aik, waqt barah."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab har tense ki pehchan wali nishaniyan samajh lo, kyunke paper me yehi nishaniyan tumhe jawab tak le jati hain. Present simple ki nishani hai roz wala waqt. Always, usually, every day, daily. Verb ki pehli form ati hai aur he, she, it ke sath s ya es lagta hai. Present continuous ki nishani hai now, at this moment, look aur listen wale jumle. Is, am, are ke sath ing wali form ati hai. Present perfect ki nishaniyan hain just, already, yet, ever, never, since aur for. Has ya have ke sath teesri form ati hai. Present perfect continuous me bhi since aur for ate hain, lekin sath waqt ki muddat lazmi hoti hai aur been ke sath ing wali form ati hai. Since subah, for do ghante."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Maazi ki nishaniyan aur saaf hain. Past simple ki nishani hai guzra hua waqt saaf likha hua. Yesterday, ago, last night, last year. Verb ki dusri form ati hai. Past continuous ki nishani hai while aur when wale jumle, jahan aik lamba kaam chal raha tha aur beech me chhota kaam aa gaya. Was ya were ke sath ing wali form. Past perfect ki pehchan ye hai ke maazi me do kaam hain aur jo pehle hua tha us par had ke sath teesri form hai. Before aur already is ki nishaniyan hain. Past perfect continuous me had been ke sath ing wali form aur muddat hoti hai. Mustaqbil ki nishaniyan sab se asaan hain. Tomorrow, next week, next year. Future simple me will ke sath pehli form, future continuous me will be ke sath ing, future perfect me by ke sath will have aur teesri form, aur future perfect continuous me will have been ke sath ing aur muddat. By wala lafz future perfect ki sab se pakki nishani hai. By Sunday, by 2030, by tomorrow."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab wo farq jo paper har saal parkhta hai. Present perfect aur past simple ka farq. Qanoon ye hai ke jab jumle me guzra hua waqt saaf likha ho, yesterday, ago ya last year, to hamesha past simple ayega, present perfect kabhi nahi ayega. I met him yesterday. Ye sahi hai. I have met him yesterday kehna ghalat hai, kyunke yesterday ate hi perfect ka darwaza band ho jata hai. Aur jab waqt na diya ho aur kaam ka asar ab bhi ho to present perfect. I have lost my key. Anaaj gum hai aur ab bhi gum hai, is liye perfect. Dusra mashhoor joda hai past continuous aur past perfect continuous ka. Dono me kaam chal raha tha, farq sirf muddat ka hai. Jab sirf ye batana ho ke us waqt kaam chal raha tha to past continuous. He was sleeping at nine. Aur jab ye batana ho ke kaam kitni muddat se chal raha tha to past perfect continuous. He had been sleeping for three hours. Muddat nazar aye to had been wala, muddat na ho to was wala."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Board par qanoon Angrezi me"),
      LessonBlock.rule("Board par ustad tense ki pehchan yun likhta hai. There are three times and four states, and three times four makes twelve tenses. The simple tense tells a fact or a habit. The continuous tense shows an action going on. The perfect tense shows an action completed. The perfect continuous tense shows an action going on for a period of time. Aur sab se aham line ye hai: when a past time like yesterday, ago or last year is given in the sentence, use the past simple, never the present perfect. Learn the signal words and the tense will name itself."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Misaalein board se"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab board par wahi barah misaalein aik sath dekho. Har misaal ke neeche us ki Urdu pehchan aur nishani likhi hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Ali reads a book every day.", note: "Urdu: Ali roz kitaab parhta hai. Nishani every day hai aur verb ki pehli form par s laga hai. Ye present simple hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Ali is reading a book now.", note: "Urdu: Ali is waqt kitaab parh raha hai. Nishani now hai aur raha hai wali awaz hai. Ye present continuous hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Ali has read the book.", note: "Urdu: Ali kitaab parh chuka hai. Chuka hai wali awaz aur has ke sath teesri form. Ye present perfect hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Ali has been reading the book since morning.", note: "Urdu: Ali subah se kitaab parh raha hai. Muddat ke sath raha hai, is liye ye present perfect continuous hai. Sirf raha hai hota to continuous tha, se wali muddat ate hi perfect continuous ban gaya."),
      LessonBlock.example("Ali read the book yesterday.", note: "Urdu: Ali ne kal kitaab parhi. Nishani yesterday hai aur verb ki dusri form read hai. Ye past simple hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Ali was reading a book when I entered the room.", note: "Urdu: Jab main kamre me dakhil hua, Ali kitaab parh raha tha. Lamba kaam chal raha tha aur beech me chhota kaam aa gaya. Ye past continuous hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Ali had read the book before I came.", note: "Urdu: Mere ane se pehle Ali kitaab parh chuka tha. Maazi ke do kaamo me pehle wale par had laga hai. Ye past perfect hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Ali had been reading the book for two hours.", note: "Urdu: Ali do ghante se kitaab parh raha tha. Maazi me muddat ke sath chal raha kaam. Ye past perfect continuous hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Ali will read the book tomorrow.", note: "Urdu: Ali kal kitaab parhega. Nishani tomorrow aur will ke sath pehli form. Ye future simple hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Ali will be reading a book at this time tomorrow.", note: "Urdu: Ali kal is waqt kitaab parh raha hoga. Raha hoga wali awaz aur will be ke sath ing. Ye future continuous hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Ali will have read the book by Sunday.", note: "Urdu: Ali itvaar tak kitaab parh chuka hoga. Nishani by hai aur will have ke sath teesri form. Ye future perfect hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Ali will have been reading the book for three hours by eight o clock.", note: "Urdu: Ali aath baje tak teen ghante se kitaab parh raha hoga. Mustaqbil me muddat ke sath chal raha kaam. Ye future perfect continuous hai, barah me sab se lamba aur sab se kam ane wala tense."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Ye kahan kaam aata hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Tense ki pehchan sirf tense wale sawal me kaam nahi ati. Voice change karna ho to pehle tense pehchanna parta hai, narration badalni ho to bhi pehle tense dekhna parta hai, aur jumla theek karne wale har sawal ki buniyad tense hi hai. Aik tarah se ye poori English grammar ki kunji hai. Jo student tense pehchan le, us ke liye agay ke sab darwaze khul jate hain."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab paper wale andaaz ke do jumle dekho."),
      LessonBlock.example("He has been teaching in this school since 2015."),
      LessonBlock.example("The train had left before we reached the station."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Pehla jumla present perfect continuous hai, since dekh kar pehchan lo. Dusra past perfect hai, station pohonchne se pehle train ja chuki thi."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Yaad rakhne ki trick"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab wo trick jo barah tenses ko aik hi nazar me pehchanwa degi. Isay Aakhir suno wali trick kehte hain. Jab bhi koi jumla samne aye, us ka Urdu tarjuma karo aur Urdu jumle ke aakhri alfaaz suno. Aakhir tumhe khud tense ka naam bata dega. Agar aakhir me ta hai, ti hai ya te hain aye to simple hai. Agar raha hai, rahi hai ya raha tha aye to continuous hai. Agar chuka hai, chuki thi ya chuka hoga aye to perfect hai. Aur agar raha hai ke sath se wali muddat bhi aye, do ghante se, subah se, to perfect continuous hai. Phir sirf waqt ka faisla baqi rehta hai ke baat haal ki hai, maazi ki ya mustaqbil ki, aur wo jumle ke isharay bata dete hain. Pehle aakhir suno, sorat pehchano. Phir waqt dekho, tense pehchano. Bas."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Paper ki aam ghaltiyan"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab wo ghaltiyan dekho jo tense ke sawalo me Pakistani students karte hain."),
      LessonBlock.trap("I have met him yesterday.", "I met him yesterday.", "yesterday ate hi present perfect khatam ho jata hai. Guzra waqt saaf likha ho to hamesha past simple."),
      LessonBlock.trap("He is suffering from fever since Monday.", "He has been suffering from fever since Monday.", "since ke sath muddat se chal raha kaam present perfect continuous me ata hai, present continuous me nahi."),
      LessonBlock.trap("When I reached the station, the train left.", "When I reached the station, the train had left.", "train ka jana station pohonchne se pehle ka kaam hai. Maazi ke pehle wale kaam par had lagta hai."),
      LessonBlock.trap("I am knowing the answer.", "I know the answer.", "know, believe, like jaisay verb halat batate hain, chal raha kaam nahi. Ye continuous me nahi ate. Lesson 19 me hum ne ye baat seekhi thi."),
      LessonBlock.trap("She has wrote a letter.", "She has written a letter.", "has aur have ke baad hamesha teesri form ati hai. Wrote dusri hai, written teesri."),
      LessonBlock.trap("He did not went to school.", "He did not go to school.", "did ate hi verb apni pehli form me wapas chala jata hai. Did ne maazi ka bojh utha liya, verb ko dusri form ki zaroorat nahi."),
      LessonBlock.trap("I have been knowing him for years.", "I have known him for years.", "know ko muddat ke sath bhi continuous nahi banate. Has known hi sahi hai."),
    ],
    mcqs: <LessonMcq>[
        LessonMcq(
          question: "\"She has been waiting for the bus for two hours.\" Ye jumla konsa tense hai?",
          options: <String>["Present continuous", "Present perfect", "Present perfect continuous", "Past perfect continuous"],
          correctIndex: 2,
          explanation: "Has been ke sath ing wali form aur for two hours ki muddat hai. Muddat ke sath chal raha kaam present perfect continuous hota hai.",
        ),
        LessonMcq(
          question: "Choose the correct sentence:",
          options: <String>["I have seen him yesterday.", "I saw him yesterday.", "I have see him yesterday.", "I am seeing him yesterday."],
          correctIndex: 1,
          explanation: "Yesterday saaf likha hai, is liye sirf past simple ayega. Aakhir suno wali trick ke sath ye paper ka sab se dohraya jane wala qanoon hai.",
        ),
        LessonMcq(
          question: "He ___ in this office since 2019.",
          options: <String>["works", "is working", "has been working", "worked"],
          correctIndex: 2,
          explanation: "Since 2019 muddat bata raha hai aur kaam ab bhi chal raha hai, is liye has been working.",
        ),
        LessonMcq(
          question: "When the teacher entered the class, the students ___ noise.",
          options: <String>["make", "were making", "have made", "will make"],
          correctIndex: 1,
          explanation: "Teacher ke ane ke waqt shor mach raha tha. Chal raha maazi ka kaam past continuous me ata hai, were making.",
        ),
        LessonMcq(
          question: "By next year, they ___ the bridge.",
          options: <String>["will build", "will have built", "are building", "built"],
          correctIndex: 1,
          explanation: "By next year future perfect ki pakki nishani hai. Will have built.",
        ),
        LessonMcq(
          question: "Choose the correct sentence:",
          options: <String>["The patient died before the doctor arrived.", "The patient had died before the doctor arrived.", "The patient has died before the doctor arrived.", "The patient die before the doctor arrived."],
          correctIndex: 1,
          explanation: "Mareez ka marna doctor ke ane se pehle ka kaam hai. Pehle wale kaam par had died ayega.",
        ),
        LessonMcq(
          question: "She ___ her homework just now. Ka sahi option chuno jab matlab ho ke kaam abhi abhi mukammal hua hai.",
          options: <String>["finishes", "is finishing", "has finished", "will finish"],
          correctIndex: 2,
          explanation: "Just now ke sath abhi mukammal hua kaam present perfect me ata hai. Has finished.",
        ),
        LessonMcq(
          question: "\"The boys were playing cricket at that time.\" Ye jumla konsa tense hai?",
          options: <String>["Past simple", "Past continuous", "Past perfect", "Present continuous"],
          correctIndex: 1,
          explanation: "Were ke sath ing wali form aur at that time ka ishara. Past continuous.",
        ),
        LessonMcq(
          question: "He ___ to school daily.",
          options: <String>["go", "goes", "going", "gone"],
          correctIndex: 1,
          explanation: "Daily aadat hai aur he, she, it wale khandan me verb par s lagta hai. Goes.",
        ),
        LessonMcq(
          question: "Choose the correct sentence:",
          options: <String>["She does not likes tea.", "She does not like tea.", "She do not like tea.", "She does not liking tea."],
          correctIndex: 1,
          explanation: "Does ate hi verb apni pehli form me ajata hai. Like sahi hai, likes ghalat.",
        ),
      ],
  ),
  Lesson(
    id: "grammar-32",
    number: 32,
    title: "Usage — Is Am Are, Has Have Had, Do Does Did",
    subtitle: "Teen Khandan. Is, has aur does kiske sath ate hain, Urdu matlab ke sath",
    partIndex: 6,
    partName: "Helping Verbs aur Modals",
    blocks: <LessonBlock>[
      LessonBlock.heading("Ye lesson kyun zaroori hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("PPSC ke one paper me agar kisi aik cheez par sab se zyada sawal bante hain to wo yehi chhote chhote helping verb hain. Is, am, are. Has, have, had. Do, does, did. Khali jagah me inhi me se aik lagana hota hai, jumla theek karna ho to inhi ki ghalti chhupi hoti hai, aur tense ka har sawal bhi inhi se shuru hota hai. Masla ye hai ke students inhe alag alag lafz samajh kar ratte hain, halanke ye sirf teen khandan hain. Jo student teen khandano ka hisaab samajh le, us ke liye English ka aadha darwaza khul jata hai. Lesson 3 me hum ne pronouns ke sath am, is, are ki pehli pehchan ki thi. Ab un teen khandano ko mukammal karte hain, Urdu matlab ke sath, taake paper me kabhi shak na ho."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Pehle teen khandan pehchano"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Dekho, ye nau alfaaz asal me teen gharano ke log hain. Pehla gharana be wala hai, is, am, are, aur is ke maazi wale rishtedar was aur were. Is gharane ka Urdu matlab hai hai, hun, hain, tha, the. Ye halat aur pehchan batata hai. Wo doctor hai, main student hun. Dusra gharana have wala hai, has, have aur had. Is ka matlab hai ke paas hona, rakhna, aur perfect tense me chuka wala kaam bhi yehi gharana uthata hai. Teesra gharana do wala hai, do, does aur did. Ye gharana khud koi matlab nahi rakhta, ye sirf sawal aur nafi banane ke liye bulaya jata hai, aur as a main verb is ka matlab hota hai karna. Teen gharane zehen me bitha lo, ab har aik ka hisaab alag alag dekhte hain."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab pehla sawal jo har khandan me poocha jata hai. Kiske sath konsa? Is ka jawab aik hi hai aur teeno khandano par lagoo hota hai. He, she, it aur koi aik naam, in ke sath khaas form ata hai. Baqi sab ke sath, I, we, you, they aur zyada cheezon ke sath, aam form ata hai. Be wale gharane me khaas form is hai aur aam form are hai, bas I beech me apna alag am rakhta hai. Have wale gharane me khaas form has hai aur aam form have hai. Do wale gharane me khaas form does hai aur aam form do hai. Aur maazi me aakar ye farq ghat jata hai. Had sab ke sath aik hi ata hai, did bhi sab ke sath aik hi ata hai. Bas be wale gharane me was aik ke sath aur were zyada ke sath, ye chhota sa farq reh jata hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab has been aur have been wali baat, jo paper ki pasandida hai. Jab has ya have ke baad been aye to do matlab nikalte hain. Aik matlab hai muddat se chal rahi halat. He has been ill since Monday. Wo Peer se beemar hai. Been ke baad ing wali form ajaye to kaam muddat se chal raha hota hai, jaisa Lesson 31 me parha tha. He has been teaching for ten years. Dusra matlab hai ja kar ana ya ja chuka hona, aur yahan been aur gone ka farq paper bohat parkhta hai. He has been to Lahore ka matlab hai wo Lahore ja kar wapas aa chuka hai. He has gone to Lahore ka matlab hai wo Lahore gaya hai aur abhi wahin hai, wapas nahi aya. Been matlab ja aya, gone matlab gaya aur abhi gaya hua hai. Ye farq zehen me nikaal kar rakh lo."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab do wale gharane ki khaas baat samajh lo, kyunke ye do chehray rakhta hai. Kabhi ye main verb hota hai, khud kaam karta hai. He does his homework daily. Yahan does ka matlab hai karta hai. She did her work. Aur kabhi ye sirf madadgar hota hai, sawal aur nafi banane ke liye. Does he play cricket? He does not play cricket. Yahan does khud koi kaam nahi kar raha, sirf asal verb play ki madad kar raha hai. Aur jab do madadgar ban kar ata hai to aik qanoon lazmi yad rakho. Does aur did apne sath asal verb ko us ki pehli form me lete hain. Does he go, did he go. Go par na s lagega, na went banega. Maazi ka aur s wala sara bojh does aur did ne khud utha liya hota hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Has wale gharane ki bhi aik do-chehri sorat hai. Jab has aur have ke baad teesri form aye to ye perfect tense banate hain. She has finished. Aur jab in ke baad koi cheez aye to ye rakhne ka matlab dete hain. She has a car. She has finished me has madadgar hai, she has a car me has khud asal verb hai. Aur is dusri sorat me sawal do se banta hai. Does she have a car? Ye jumla paper me aksar ata hai aur aksar galat kiya jata hai."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Board par qanoon Angrezi me"),
      LessonBlock.rule("Board par ustad ye lines likhta hai. There are three families: be, have and do. With he, she, it and a singular name, use is, has and does. With I, we, you and they, use have and do, and am or are for be. In the past, had and did are the same for every subject. After has and have, the main verb is always in its third form. After do, does and did, the main verb is always in its first form. Aur aakhri line: has been to a place means went and returned; has gone to a place means went and is still there."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Misaalein board se"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab board par misaalein dekho. Har misaal ke sath us ki wajah bhi samjho."),
      LessonBlock.example("She is a doctor.", note: "Is aya kyunke she khaas khandan me hai. Urdu matlab hai wo doctor hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("I am a student of this college.", note: "I ke sath hamesha am ata hai. Ye be wale gharane ka woh wahid farq hai jo ratna parta hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("They have two sons.", note: "They ke sath have aya. Matlab hai un ke do bete hain, yani wo rakhte hain."),
      LessonBlock.example("He has been ill since Monday.", note: "Has ke baad been aur since ke sath muddat. Matlab hai wo Peer se beemar hai, halat chal rahi hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("My father has gone to Karachi.", note: "Gone aya hai, matlab hai wo Karachi gaye hain aur abhi wahin hain, wapas nahi aye."),
      LessonBlock.example("My father has been to Karachi many times.", note: "Been aya hai, matlab hai wo kayi dafa Karachi ja kar wapas aa chuke hain. Gone aur been ka yahi farq paper me ata hai."),
      LessonBlock.example("Does your brother work in a bank?", note: "Does madadgar ban kar aya hai, is liye asal verb work apni pehli form me hai. Works nahi likha."),
      LessonBlock.example("He does his homework in the evening.", note: "Yahan does khud main verb hai, matlab karta hai. Pichhli misaal se farq dekh lo, wahan does sirf madadgar tha."),
      LessonBlock.example("Did you sleep well last night?", note: "Did sab ke sath aik hi ata hai aur us ke baad pehli form sleep hai. Slept nahi aya."),
      LessonBlock.example("We had a small house in our village last year.", note: "Had have wale gharane ki maazi shakal hai, sab ke sath aik jaisi. Matlab hai hamare paas tha."),
      LessonBlock.example("She has written three letters.", note: "Has ke baad teesri form written hai. Ye perfect tense hai, has yahan rakhne wala matlab nahi de raha."),
      LessonBlock.example("Does she have a car?", note: "Has wali dusri sorat ka sawal do se banta hai aur have apni pehli form me rehta hai. Ye jumla paper ka pasandida hai."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Ye kahan kaam aata hai"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Rozmarra ki har baat inhi teen khandano se banti hai. Tum kya karte ho, us ke paas kya hai, wo kahan tha, ye sawal poochna ho ya nafi karni ho, har jagah yehi alfaaz kaam ate hain. Daftar ki darkhwast ho ya dost se guftagu, is, has aur does ka sahi mel hi tumhari English ko sahi ya ghalat banata hai. Paper me to ye haal hai ke har dusra sawal inhi ke gird ghoomta hai."),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab paper wale andaaz ke do jumle dekho."),
      LessonBlock.example("He has been serving in this department for fifteen years."),
      LessonBlock.example("Does the committee have any objection to this proposal?"),
      LessonBlock.heading("Yaad rakhne ki trick"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab wo trick jo teen khandano ko aik line me bandh degi. Isay S wale teen dost kehte hain. Gaur karo, he, she, it ke sath ane wale teeno khaas formon me s ata hai. Is, has, does. Teeno me s ki awaz hai. Aur ye teen dost sirf teen mehmaano ke ghar jate hain, he, she aur it ke ghar, ya kisi aik naam ke ghar. Baqi sab ke darwaze par aam form khare hain, are, have aur do, jin me s nahi hai. To jab bhi shak ho, pehle dekho subject he, she, it hai ya koi aik naam. Hai to s wala dost bulao, is, has ya does. Nahi hai to baghair s wala form lagao, are, have ya do. Aur maazi me to jhagra hi khatam, had aur did har ghar me aik jaise jate hain. Bas ye yaad rakho, s wale teen dost sirf he, she, it ke dost hain."),
      LessonBlock.heading("Paper ki aam ghaltiyan"),
      LessonBlock.paragraph("Ab wo ghaltiyan dekho jo in teen khandano me Pakistani students karte hain."),
      LessonBlock.trap("Does he goes to school?", "Does he go to school?", "does ne s wala bojh khud utha liya hai. Us ke baad verb apni pehli form me ayega, goes nahi, go."),
      LessonBlock.trap("She has went to Lahore.", "She has gone to Lahore.", "has ke baad teesri form ati hai. Went dusri form hai, gone teesri."),
      LessonBlock.trap("Did you went to the bazaar?", "Did you go to the bazaar?", "did ke baad hamesha pehli form. Did khud maazi hai, verb ko maazi banane ki zaroorat nahi."),
      LessonBlock.trap("He do not have a pen.", "He does not have a pen.", "he ke sath do wala khaas form does ata hai, do nahi. S wale teen dost wali baat yaad hai na?"),
      LessonBlock.trap("I am agree with you.", "I agree with you.", "agree khud aik verb hai, us ke aage am lagana ghalti hai. Ye ghalti Urdu ke \"main raazi hun\" wale asar se hoti hai."),
      LessonBlock.trap("She is having two brothers.", "She has two brothers.", "rakhne ke matlab me have ko continuous me nahi rakhte. Has two brothers hi sahi hai."),
